WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.127 --> 00:00:01.840
- And you actually have
your own story, right,

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.790
that you're bringing to the table.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.660
And I find insanely possible.
- Thanks!

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.530
- Like, go ahead and tell everybody.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.363
They're not going to believe you.

00:00:07.363 --> 00:00:10.576
- Yeah, so I weighed 322
pounds about five years ago.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:15.090
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.210
- Like, that's incredible.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.043
- Thank you.

00:00:18.043 --> 00:00:19.290
So, you know, weighing that

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.330
and then coming to be a
trainer on The Biggest Loser

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.950
five years later is just insane.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.440
But you know I'm a single mom.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.174
I just beat stage II
thyroid cancer this year.

00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:28.007
- Wow!

00:00:28.007 --> 00:00:29.340
Congratulations!

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.560
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.280
Wow, you have had quite a life.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.620
- [Lugo] Yeah, so.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.030
- Just hurdle and hurdle and yeah.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:36.947
- Yeah.
- Yup.

00:00:36.947 --> 00:00:37.780
- And I feel like everything's

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:38.730
kind of brought me to this point.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.120
And to share that experience

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.150
and what I've gone through
with the contestants,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.690
I've had to relive that.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.290
And I get what they're going through.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.770
So, for me, it's such a fulfilling thing

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.650
to be like, "I get it."

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.360
Like those tears you're crying?

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.330
I've cried those tears.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.900
Like that burpee you're complaining about?

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.700
I've also cried with that burpee.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.780
- Oh my god, I hate burpees.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.370
It's like the devil's work.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.384
- Yes it is.

00:00:59.384 --> 00:01:01.070
- It's true though.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.340
I mean, it's completely different

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.430
but the analogy of it is

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.660
everybody always asks me about The Voice,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.493
what I love about The Voice.

00:01:05.493 --> 00:01:06.326
It's the same thing.

00:01:06.326 --> 00:01:07.520
I've actually been in their shoes.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.080
And when you're actually
trying to coach someone

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.270
that you've been in their shoes,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.190
you feel like you have
some kind of connection

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.830
that maybe everybody can't have, you know?

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.930
So that's probably, coming
from you, that means a lot.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:17.763
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:19.670
That you've been able
to shed all that weight

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.638
and like change your life.
- Yeah.

00:01:20.638 --> 00:01:24.610
She really put her heart
all over the gym floor

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.311
every moment that she was there.

00:01:26.311 --> 00:01:30.550
She's the real deal, she really
delivered every single day.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.210
And we're just so lucky to have her.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.043
- Oh my god.

00:01:33.043 --> 00:01:34.987
The combination of this is awesome.

00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:35.820
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.363
So but you're bringing a
new perspective, right?

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.270
'Cause you had a heart attack, right?

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.910
- I did, it's been almost three years now.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.047
I had a heart attack when I
was living in New York City.

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:45.910
And not only did I have a heart attack,

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.180
but I went into cardiac arrest.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.450
So I felt a Biggest Loser
contestant during my recovery

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.800
because I went from doing CrossFit

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.970
and being able to work
out so hard all the time

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.970
to not being able to
walk around a city block

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.270
without feeling winded.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.210
Had to change everything
about the way that I ate.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.530
And everything about the
way that I worked out.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.770
And as I was going through my
rehab I was just like, wow.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.930
This is what it feels like
to start back at square one.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.140
And that's what I've gone through.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:15.973
- Gosh.

00:02:15.973 --> 00:02:18.300
Once again, though, it means so much more.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.213
I know that sucks having
had to go through that.

00:02:20.213 --> 00:02:22.560
- It's the worst gift you could ever get.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.393
But you know what?

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:24.226
You make something out of it.

00:02:24.226 --> 00:02:25.560
- Yeah, you can relate to them, though.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.587
Like people you can relate and say

00:02:26.587 --> 00:02:28.270
"Hey, I've had to work
from the ground up, too."

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.620
It means something
different when you say that.

